@page
@model SpaceGeeks.Pages.NasaMissionsModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Important NASA Missions";
}

<div class="container">
    <h1>Important NASA Missions Through History</h1>
    
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-12">
            <p>NASA has launched numerous missions that have expanded our understanding of space and our solar system. Here are some of the most significant missions:</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mission-timeline">
        <div class="mission-item">
            <h3>Apollo Program (1961-1972)</h3>
            <p>Landed the first humans on the Moon. Apollo 11 successfully landed on July 20, 1969, with Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin becoming the first humans to walk on the lunar surface.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mission-item">
            <h3>Voyager 1 and 2 (1977)</h3>
            <p>Explored the outer planets and are now in interstellar space. Voyager 1 became the first human-made object to enter interstellar space in 2012.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mission-item">
            <h3>Hubble Space Telescope (1990-present)</h3>
            <p>Has provided unprecedented views of the universe, contributing to major discoveries about the age and expansion of the universe.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mission-item">
            <h3>Mars Rovers (1997-present)</h3>
            <p>Starting with Sojourner, followed by Spirit, Opportunity, Curiosity, and Perseverance, these rovers have explored the Martian surface and searched for signs of past life.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mission-item">
            <h3>Cassini-Huygens (1997-2017)</h3>
            <p>Studied Saturn and its moons, particularly Titan. The mission revealed detailed information about Saturn's rings and discovered liquid methane lakes on Titan.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mission-item">
            <h3>James Webb Space Telescope (2021-present)</h3>
            <p>Successor to Hubble, designed to observe the most distant objects in the universe and study the formation of galaxies, stars, and planetary systems.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>